{
  "abstract": "Lean 4 formalization of Theorems 1.1, 1.3 and 1.4 of the paper \"Structured coordinate systems in Lᵖ(ℝ)\" by D. Freeman, L. Liehr and M. A. Taylor (arXiv:2610.18709v2). For every 1 ≤ p < ∞ and every ε > 0 there is a Schauder basis of Lᵖ(ℝ) that consists of non-negative functions and has basis constant less than 1 + ε, and no Schauder basis of non-negative functions has basis constant 1. For every 2 ≤ p < ∞ there are a nonzero real-valued function f ∈ Lᵖ(ℝ) and real numbers λₙ such that the translates f(· − λₙ) form a Schauder basis of Lᵖ(ℝ), over the real and over the complex scalars. For p = 2 and every ε > 0, the function f can be chosen such that it extends to an entire function and the basis constant is less than 1 + ε. For p > 2 and every unbounded set S ⊆ ℝ, the function f can be chosen non-negative and such that it extends to an entire function, with all λₙ in S.",
  "authors": [
